Sval: deprecation warnings are not shown for the application's own documents

A deprecated WebIDL member warns once per document that uses it. Firefox's
browser chrome reads Window.fullScreen across its own scripts, so every
browser window would log "Window.fullScreen attribute is deprecated" to the
user's console. The warning is for the authors of web pages, which still get
it. The many chrome call sites are Mozilla's, so the one place every
deprecation is shown is changed instead.

diff --git a/dom/bindings/BindingUtils.cpp b/dom/bindings/BindingUtils.cpp
index f7188c8585..204169ac5c 100644
--- a/dom/bindings/BindingUtils.cpp
+++ b/dom/bindings/BindingUtils.cpp
@@ -4040,8 +4040,12 @@ void MaybeShowDeprecationWarning(const GlobalObject& aGlobal,
   if (NS_IsMainThread()) {
     nsCOMPtr<nsPIDOMWindowInner> window =
         do_QueryInterface(aGlobal.GetAsSupports());
-    if (window && window->GetExtantDoc()) {
-      window->GetExtantDoc()->WarnOnceAbout(aOperation);
+    Document* doc = window ? window->GetExtantDoc() : nullptr;
+    // A deprecation warning is for the authors of web pages. The
+    // application's own chrome documents read deprecated attributes such as
+    // Window.fullScreen by design.
+    if (doc && !doc->NodePrincipal()->IsSystemPrincipal()) {
+      doc->WarnOnceAbout(aOperation);
     }
     return;
   }
